    "image_with_text_tifzJx": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_PN7iyh": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Should You Use Reflective Tape in the Workplace?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_qxYxdg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) and other government agencies require industrial and commercial facilities to mark floors and other potentially hazardous locations with tape to prevent workplace injury. The tape markings inform facility employees and visitors of dangers they may encounter within the facility and how to avoid them, which can result in improved workplace safety.</p><p>Other purposes of reflective safety tapes in workplaces include:</p><ul><li>Guiding the flow of traffic within the facility</li><li>Highlighting pathways to entrances/exits when the power is out</li><li>Increasing worker visibility with patches on clothing and PPE</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_PN7iyh",
        "text_qxYxdg"
      ],
